# Base egress allowlist for every devbox sandbox.
#
# One entry per line, `#` starts a comment. An entry is an exact host
# (`example.com`, port 443 assumed), a host with a port (`example.com:8080`), a
# single-label wildcard (`*.example.com` — one label, so not `a.b.example.com`),
# or a CIDR. sbx enforces the first three today and accepts the rest as declared.
#
# This file is the *floor*: what the image's own toolchain needs. Two other
# things add to it, and neither belongs here:
#
#   projects/<profile>/allowed-domains        merged for the matching workspace
#   DEVBOX_ALLOW_DOMAINS=a.example b.example  one-off, at `devbox up` time
#
# scripts/build-kit.sh merges the three into `permissions.network.allow` in the
# generated kit, and `sbx create --kit` applies it to the sandbox. Changing any
# of them takes effect on `devbox rebuild` — a kit's rules are chosen at create
# time, so a restart is no longer enough. Confirm what landed with
# `devbox status`, which prints the sandbox's active policy.
#
# It is only an allowlist if the machine denies by default. A kit's rules are
# added on top of the global policy, so under `allow-all` egress is open and
# every line here is decoration:
#
#   sbx policy init deny-all
#
# Anthropic's own hosts are NOT here: the built-in `claude` kit declares
# api.anthropic.com, platform.claude.com, claude.com, downloads.claude.ai,
# mcp-proxy.anthropic.com and bridge.claudeusercontent.com, and sbx merges its
# list with this one. Only what that kit misses is listed below.
#
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/network-config#network-access-requirements

# --- GitHub -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Also the five domains the kit's `github` credential injects into, and the spec
# requires every one of those to appear in an allow list.
github.com
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
raw.githubusercontent.com
objects.githubusercontent.com

# --- Node / package registries ------------------------------------------------
registry.npmjs.org
registry.yarnpkg.com
repo.yarnpkg.com
nodejs.org

# --- Claude Code --------------------------------------------------------------
# What the built-in kit's own list leaves out: error reporting, and the feature
# gates. Claude Code's telemetry host is statsig.anthropic.com, but that name has
# no public A record; it lands on Statsig's CDN, which these two cover.
sentry.io
statsig.com
featuregates.org

# --- Playwright ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Where `playwright install` fetches browser builds from. The CDN moved hosts
# between versions, so all three are listed. The download lands in the shared
# ~/.cache/devbox/ms-playwright, so it happens once for every workspace.
cdn.playwright.dev
playwright.azureedge.net
playwright.download.prss.microsoft.com

# --- The host machine ---------------------------------------------------------
# The one route out of the VM to something running on this machine. Claude Code's
# OTLP export uses it (scripts/build-kit.sh), and the rocketchat profile reaches
# the shared MongoDB over it.
#
# Nothing on the host is reachable without a published port on the host side: the
# sandbox has its own network namespace, so `localhost` in here is the VM.
host.docker.internal

# --- Editors ------------------------------------------------------------------
# For attaching VS Code over `sbx setup ssh`, which downloads its own server into
# the sandbox on first connect.
marketplace.visualstudio.com
vscode.blob.core.windows.net
update.code.visualstudio.com
